    "explanation": "The TLS certificate for ledger-gateway.internal.example expired at about midnight UTC on 2026-11-12, and that broke settlements. cert-renewer tried to renew it on 11-10 and 11-11, failed both times because DNS validation timed out, then gave up after the maximum number of attempts (LOG-0002-0001, -0002, -0003). From 00:00:04 on 11-12, every payments-worker call to ledger-gateway failed with 'TLS handshake failed: certificate has expired' (LOG-0002-0010 and later). The worker retried, then moved each batch to the dead-letter queue. That drove the 97% error rate (LOG-0002-0032) and the queue backlog. Finance's ticket also says no settlements have been confirmed since just after midnight (TKT-0002). The DNS timeouts explain why renewal failed, but the trigger is the expired certificate: renewing or replacing it ends the incident. The long GC pauses are unrelated noise.",
